/E (Human Interaction with Other Living BeingsIn everyday life, humans are constantly connected to other living creatures. We depend on plants for oxygen, food, and natural resources. Agriculture is a clear example of this relationship, where humans grow crops and rely on animals like bees to pollinate them. Without these interactions, food production would not be possible.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
321 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 116 0 R
/E (Pets such as dogs and cats are also part of human life. They provide comfort, companionship, and emotional support. On the other hand, some living creatures, like mosquitoes or flies, can cause discomfort or spread diseases. These different interactions show that the relationship between humans and other living beings can be both positive and negative, but it is always important.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [7]
>>
