<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 117 0 R
/E (When people think about living creatures, they often imagine wild forests or distant oceans. However, life exists all around us, even in cities and neighborhoods. Humans share their daily environment with many other living beings such as birds, insects, plants, and small animals. For example, pigeons fly between buildings, cats roam the streets, and ants live in small colonies on sidewalks.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
331 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 117 0 R
/E (These living creatures have adapted to urban life in remarkable ways. Birds may build their nests on rooftops instead of trees, while some animals survive by finding food in human waste. Plants grow in parks, gardens, and even between cracks in the pavement. This shows that nature is not separate from us; it exists beside us and adapts to our way of life.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
