<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 118 0 R
/E (The world of living creatures today faces many real-life challenges, especially due to human activities. Pollution from cars, factories, and waste affects air, water, and soil, harming both animals and plants. In addition, the expansion of cities leads to the destruction of natural habitats, forcing many species to disappear.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
347 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 118 0 R
/E (Despite these problems, individuals can take simple actions to help protect living creatures. Reducing waste, recycling, and limiting the use of plastic can make a big difference. Planting trees and protecting green spaces also support life in urban areas. By being more responsible in our daily actions, we can help create a healthier environment.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
348 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 118 0 R
/E (In conclusion, living creatures are an essential part of our daily lives. Humans are not separate from nature but are deeply connected to it. By understanding this connection and taking small steps, we can help protect the world of living beings for future generations.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
