361 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 119 0 R
/E (Did you know that bananas are technically berries, but strawberries are not? Botanically, a berry develops from a single ovary and must have seeds embedded inside the flesh. By that definition, bananas, cucumbers, and even watermelons qualify as berries, while strawberrie with their seeds on the outside  belong to a different category altogether.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
