/S /P
/P 119 0 R
/E (Did you know that a day on Venus is longer than a year on Venus? The planet takes about 243 Earth days to rotate once on its axis, but only about 225 Earth days to complete one orbit around the Sun. If you lived there, you would experience fewer birthdays than sunrises.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [13]
>>
