426 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E (Social media made comparison faster, easier, and completely inescapable. Someone is always doing better, looking better, achieving more at least from the outside.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
427 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E (But here's what the highlight reel never shows. The person whose grades you envy cried over that same subject two weeks ago. The one who looks effortlessly confident has a whole internal dialogue you'd never guess from their Instagram. Everyone is fighting something invisible. Everyone.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
428 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E (Comparison also has this sneaky way of making you compete in races you never actually signed up for. Suddenly you feel behind on a timeline that was never yours to begin with someone else's definition of success quietly became the standard you're measuring yourself against without even noticing.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
429 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 124 0 R
/E (The only comparison worth making is between who you were last month and who you are now. That's the only race where winning actually means something to your life.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
